{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270540",
      "title": "Avoiding Component Function Executions with Clever Structuring",
      "sourceHash": "19e7d174655b34b3b4cf9d2d58faeade39e144f54cb5f3f12ac6d4932453642a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "So 'memo', if used with care, can be useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "but it's not the only way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "of preventing unnecessary renders here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 14.03,
          "en": "Another technique that is often even more powerful than memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.13,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "is a clever component composition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 18.783,
          "en": "in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "For example here, I have this section with that input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "where we register every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "and change the state with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 30.723,
          "en": "in this app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.59,
          "end": 35.85,
          "en": "Now of course, we could put this into a separate component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.85,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "and then this state that changes on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "would also live in that separate component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 46.353,
          "en": "and would not affect this app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 50.01,
          "en": "So here we could add a separate component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.01,
          "end": 52.01,
          "en": "which could be named 'ConfigureCounter',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.4,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 59.68,
          "en": "where I export my 'ConfigureCounter' component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 65.85,
          "en": "and we can then grab this section code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.85,
          "end": 70.5,
          "en": "from the app component, cut it, and return it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.5,
          "end": 75.5,
          "en": "in 'ConfigureCounter' and also grab this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 81.15,
          "en": "and copy that and add it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "Though we don't need the chosen count state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 85.413,
          "en": "just the entered number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "And now we just need to lift some state up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "So that of course when that number that was entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "is confirmed by clicking this set button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "We propagate this information from 'ConfigureCounter'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 106.38,
          "en": "to the app component because that state will be needed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.38,
          "end": 108.42,
          "en": "so that it can be passed down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "to the counter component where it will in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 112.083,
          "en": "then be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "And therefore in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 117.63,
          "en": "we can get rid of these functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "and of the 'EnteredNumber' state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 122.05,
          "en": "But we must keep the 'ChosenCount' state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123,
          "end": 126.02,
          "en": "and we should now add a new function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.02,
          "end": 129.843,
          "en": "'handleSetCount' could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 134.49,
          "en": "where we expect to get the new count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 135.573,
          "en": "as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 141.347,
          "en": "And where we then call 'setChosenCount'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.194,
          "end": 144.303,
          "en": "and set 'newCount' as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.862,
          "end": 148.973,
          "en": "And we should use 'ConfigureCounter' here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 153.933,
          "en": "and of course therefore also import it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "And then on 'ConfigureCounter', we must set a prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "through which we can pass this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 165.15,
          "en": "So that this function here can be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.15,
          "end": 167.57999999999998,
          "en": "from inside 'ConfigureCounter',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.57999999999998,
          "end": 170.823,
          "en": "a pattern we used many times before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "So we could name this prop 'onSet'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.487,
          "en": "and point at 'handleSetCount'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "And then in 'ConfigureCounter'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 183.33,
          "en": "we can destructure this 'onSet' prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 185.133,
          "en": "or whichever name you chose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 189.933,
          "en": "And we must import 'useState' of course from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.37,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "And now here in 'handleSetClick'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "instead of calling set chosen count,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 198.813,
          "en": "we can call 'onSet' here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.77,
          "end": 203.23,
          "en": "and pass the entered number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 207.39,
          "en": "as a value to that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.39,
          "end": 209.637,
          "en": "So in the end, two 'handleSetCount'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.26,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "And by doing that we now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 218.1,
          "en": "that this state that does change on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "lives in this separate component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 224.31,
          "en": "And therefore causes this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.31,
          "end": 225.873,
          "en": "to be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.13,
          "end": 230.79,
          "en": "But the app component function will not execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.79,
          "end": 234.24,
          "en": "on every keystroke in this 'ConfigureCounter' component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.24,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "because, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 240.42,
          "en": "state changes and re-executions of child components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.42,
          "end": 243.423,
          "en": "don't trigger parent component executions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "To visualize this, I'll add this log function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "which must be imported from the log JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 256.437,
          "en": "to output 'ConfigureCounter'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 261,
          "en": "And this will be on level one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 264.063,
          "en": "Because it's one level below the app component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 265.11,
          "end": 269.16,
          "en": "And if I save that all and I reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.16,
          "end": 273.18,
          "en": "you see that 'ConfigureCounter' is executed initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.18,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "But if I now clear this and I change this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 279.27,
          "en": "it's just 'ConfigureCounter' that's being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 279.27,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "The app component is not executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "The header which was executed before is not executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.053,
          "en": "And of course the counter also is not executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 294.42,
          "en": "And now here we could and should actually also remove memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 294.42,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "from the counter because now memo is useless here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "Because the app component now isn't executed anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 304.86,
          "en": "when we enter a new value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 309.06,
          "en": "but it will be executed when 'ChosenCount' gets updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 309.06,
          "end": 311.85,
          "en": "So when we click this set button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 311.85,
          "end": 313.38,
          "en": "But when that happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 313.38,
          "end": 317.7,
          "en": "we also will always re-execute the counter function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 317.7,
          "end": 321.3,
          "en": "because 'ChosenCount' is received as a prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 321.3,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "and therefore the memo check will find a different value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 326.55,
          "en": "most likely,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.55,
          "end": 330.18,
          "en": "unless we entered the same counter value as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330.18,
          "end": 332.49,
          "en": "Which would be one scenario where memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 332.49,
          "end": 334.44,
          "en": "still could be useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 334.44,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "but in most cases it won't be useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 338.7,
          "en": "because we'll have a different value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 338.7,
          "end": 340.59000000000003,
          "en": "And therefore here we could argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 340.59000000000003,
          "end": 342.39,
          "en": "that memo should be removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.39,
          "end": 344.55,
          "en": "because it's not going to prevent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.55,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "many counter function executions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 350.61,
          "en": "But it will of course always perform this check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.61,
          "end": 353.67,
          "en": "which also costs performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 353.67,
          "end": 355.2,
          "en": "Here, I'll leave it around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.2,
          "end": 358.23,
          "en": "so that you still see how it could be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 358.23,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "But be aware of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 362.28,
          "en": "that here you could consider removing memo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 362.28,
          "end": 364.713,
          "en": "because it doesn't make too much sense here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}